ne segment $\\overset{―}{EF}$ has endpoints at $E(1,1)$ and $F(2,3).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{E}^{′}{F}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${E}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{F}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$"] [:db/cas 17592186295200 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{EF}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${E}^{′}(5,5)$ and ${F}^{′}(10,15).$" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{EF}:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${E}^{′}(5,5)$ and ${F}^{′}(10,15).$"] [:db/cas 17592186295201 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ has endpoints at $Y(2,-2)$ and $Z(0,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{Z}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ has endpoints at $Y(2,-2)$ and $Z(0,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{Z}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$"] [:db/cas 17592186295201 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{YZ}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${Y}^{′}(4,-4)$ and ${Z}^{′}(0,3).$" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{YZ}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{YZ}:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${Y}^{′}(4,-4)$ and ${Z}^{′}(0,3).$"] [:db/cas 17592186295202 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(1,3),\\,Q(5,-1),$ and $R(-2,4).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(1,3),\\,Q(5,-1),$ and $R(-2,4).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$"] [:db/cas 17592186295202 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 16 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(0,6),$\n${Q}^{′}(16,-2),$ ${R}^{′}(-10,8).$" "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 16 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(0,6),$\n${Q}^{′}(16,-2),$ ${R}^{′}(-10,8).$"] [:db/cas 17592186295203 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $XYZ$ has vertices at $X(2,0),\\,Y(-4,2),$ and $Z(4,0).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{X}^{′}{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}$, the image of $△XYZ$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${X}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{Z}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $XYZ$ has vertices at $X(2,0),\\,Y(-4,2),$ and $Z(4,0).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{X}^{′}{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}$, the image of $△XYZ$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${X}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{Z}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$"] [:db/cas 17592186295203 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△XYZ$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $XYZ:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -12 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{X}^{′}{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}$ are ${X}^{′}(2,4),$\n${Y}^{′}(-12,-2),$ ${Z}^{′}(4,8).$" "To find the image of $△XYZ$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $XYZ:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -12 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{X}^{′}{Y}^{′}{Z}^{′}$ are ${X}^{′}(2,4),$\n${Y}^{′}(-12,-2),$ ${Z}^{′}(4,8).$"] [:db/cas 17592186295204 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$"] [:db/cas 17592186295204 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{′}(18,8),$ ${R}^{′}(-8,-4).$" "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{′}(18,8),$ ${R}^{′}(-8,-4).$"] [:db/cas 17592186295205 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $GHI$ has vertices at $G(5,5),\\,H(-1,-4),$ and $I(3,5).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$, the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${G}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{H}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{I}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $GHI$ has vertices at $G(5,5),\\,H(-1,-4),$ and $I(3,5).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$, the image of $△GHI$ under 